      "writtenOn": "2023-07-31T12:04:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "aptx_voice allows to set or reset Aptx SWB.\n```\nbt_status_t enable_aptx_swb_codec(bool enable) {\n  if (bluetooth::common::init_flags::aptx_voice_is_enabled()) {\n    LOG_INFO(\"%d\", enable);\n    aptx_swb_codec_status \u003d enable;\n    return BT_STATUS_SUCCESS;\n  }\n  return BT_STATUS_FAIL;\n}\n```\n\nAFAIK aptx_swb_power_management was supposed to manage enabling/disabling AptX SWB for calls:\n```\nHandle SWB codec selection based on network type\nand codecs selected over network during call\ninitiation.\n```\n\nWithout aptx_swb_power_management enabled, the AptX SWB can still be enabled/disabled for some scenarios (e.g. speech recognition).",
